WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.304
This is the AI Learning Studio: the website that runs alongside your live training.

2
00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:06.751
Let's take a quick tour.

3
00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:12.044
You open the studio in your browser, on a laptop, tablet or phone.

4
00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.405
No account, no app.

5
00:00:13.405 --> 00:00:20.962
The overview shows your three-day journey, and 'Continue your learning' takes you straight to your next block.

6
00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:24.359
Under Learning path, choose a day.

7
00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:28.867
You'll see the timetable and all eight blocks of that day.

8
00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:30.853
Click a block to open it.

9
00:00:31.653 --> 00:00:40.227
Every block starts with what you'll be able to do afterwards, followed by the phase bar: six phases, each with its time.

10
00:00:40.227 --> 00:00:43.229
Your trainer leads you through them live.

11
00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:45.944
The website is your shared workspace.

12
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:51.320
In each phase you'll find the case, your task, and a writing field.

13
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.301
Type your answer right here.

14
00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:57.195
It's your thinking that counts, so short notes are fine.

15
00:00:57.995 --> 00:01:06.110
In the Apply phase, pick your variant: A for beginners, B for leadership, C for engineering and IT.

16
00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.406
Same case, different depth.

17
00:01:09.206 --> 00:01:14.464
At the end, save your worksheet and reflection, and mark the block as complete.

18
00:01:14.464 --> 00:01:17.060
Your progress on the overview updates.

19
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.857
It's for you, not a grade.

20
00:01:19.657 --> 00:01:25.155
The Case studio holds eight case cards and two role simulations, all synthetic.

21
00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:30.028
Search or filter, and open a card when your trainer starts the round.

22
00:01:30.828 --> 00:01:34.666
Each card states your task and the expected output.

23
00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:40.612
Write down your evidence, unknowns, decision, owner and next check, then save.

24
00:01:40.612 --> 00:01:43.999
The debrief happens live, with your trainer.

25
00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:48.649
The Decision toolkit helps you compare options.

26
00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:54.710
Rate each of the eight criteria from one to five, or leave it as unknown.

27
00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.250
Unknowns are information, too.

28
00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.665
And remember: a gate is not a score.

29
00:02:00.665 --> 00:02:08.222
If a mandatory requirement is unresolved or blocked, there's no recommendation, however high the total.

30
00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:13.381
The toolkit also includes a decision record and the five tool classes.

31
00:02:14.181 --> 00:02:16.607
My workbook is where transfer happens.

32
00:02:16.607 --> 00:02:22.991
Pick your function, then note your task, its boundary, your verification check, and your next step.

33
00:02:23.791 --> 00:02:28.215
Below, plan your thirty, sixty and ninety day follow-up.

34
00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:35.562
Then save it, and use 'Export saved workbook' to keep a copy you can print or save as a PDF.

35
00:02:36.362 --> 00:02:47.973
Under Resources, you'll find the participant workbook as a PDF, the AI literacy survey toolkit, the Grid Ops Lab practice dashboard, and checked reference reading.

36
00:02:48.773 --> 00:02:52.222
One last thing: your notes stay in this browser.

37
00:02:52.222 --> 00:02:54.018
Trainers can't see them.

38
00:02:54.018 --> 00:03:00.341
So use synthetic data only, and export before you switch devices or clear your browser.

39
00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:01.131
That's it.

40
00:03:01.131 --> 00:03:02.424
Enjoy the course.
